ng CYP2A6. These enzyme modulations can alter the pharmacokinetics of co-administered drugs, particularly those with narrow therapeutic indices such as warfarin. The evidence also notes that its impact on CYP enzymes may vary depending on dosage and combination regimens, underscoring the need for careful clinical monitoring during polypharmacy [Data: Relationships (3047, 30738)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"热毒宁注射液 is frequently co-administered with beta-lactam antibiotics for enhanced efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Clinical practice commonly pairs 热毒宁注射液 with beta-lactam antibiotics, particularly cephalosporins such as 头孢唑肟 and 头孢替唑钠. Evidence from邓学灵[14] demonstrates that联合 therapy with 头孢替唑钠 and 热毒宁注射液 reduces fever time in children with acute bronchitis from 20.34 hours (monotherapy) to 12.18 hours (combination). Similar benefits are reported with 头孢唑肟 in severe pneumonia cases. This pattern of use reflects a broader trend of integrating traditional Chinese medicine injections with conventional antimicrobials to improve symptom resolution and reduce adverse reactions [Data: Relationships (43452, 43454, 23020, 23025)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"热毒宁注射液 is used in the context of COVID-19 treatment protocols\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Although not directly indicated for 新型冠状病毒肺炎 in all datasets, 热毒宁注射液 appears within the broader therapeutic landscape of the pandemic. It is listed among traditional Chinese medicines evaluated during the early phases of the outbreak when no specific antivirals were available. The第七版诊疗方案 retained many herbal formulations from earlier versions, suggesting continued clinical relevance. While direct efficacy data against SARS-CoV-2 is not detailed in the provided evidence, its inclusion in national guidelines implies recognition of its potential supportive role in managing viral pneumonia and inflammatory responses [Data: Entities (1219); Relationships (64339)]. Note: